WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.700
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.027
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.327 --> 00:00:14.090
Unit nine: Smart Shopping. In this unit, you will talk about shopping, products and consumer choices.

4
00:00:15.083 --> 00:00:16.015
counterfeit.

5
00:00:16.715 --> 00:00:19.504
counterfeit means fake; made to look like the real product.

6
00:00:19.804 --> 00:00:22.303
The police found hundreds of counterfeit watches.

7
00:00:23.003 --> 00:00:25.307
Your turn. Say: counterfeit.

8
00:00:28.007 --> 00:00:28.961
counterfeit.

9
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:30.870
second-hand.

10
00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:34.405
second-hand means not new; owned by someone before.

11
00:00:34.705 --> 00:00:37.285
I bought a second-hand bike for twenty dollars.

12
00:00:37.985 --> 00:00:40.255
Your turn. Say: second-hand.

13
00:00:42.955 --> 00:00:43.956
second-hand.

14
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.079
impulse buy.

15
00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:49.765
impulse buy means something you buy suddenly without planning.

16
00:00:50.065 --> 00:00:52.785
These sunglasses were an impulse buy at the airport.

17
00:00:53.485 --> 00:00:56.218
Your turn. Say: impulse buy.

18
00:00:58.918 --> 00:01:00.198
impulse buy.

19
00:01:01.183 --> 00:01:02.498
price comparison.

20
00:01:03.198 --> 00:01:06.974
price comparison means checking the price of a product in different shops.

21
00:01:07.274 --> 00:01:10.132
A quick price comparison saved me thirty dollars.

22
00:01:10.832 --> 00:01:13.554
Your turn. Say: price comparison.

23
00:01:16.254 --> 00:01:17.592
price comparison.

24
00:01:18.583 --> 00:01:19.851
customer review.

25
00:01:20.551 --> 00:01:24.130
customer review means an opinion written by someone who bought a product.

26
00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.347
I always read customer reviews before I buy online.

27
00:01:28.047 --> 00:01:30.896
Your turn. Say: customer review.

28
00:01:33.596 --> 00:01:34.806
customer review.

29
00:01:35.817 --> 00:01:36.864
online order.

30
00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:40.272
online order means a purchase made on the internet.

31
00:01:40.572 --> 00:01:43.106
My online order was delivered in two days.

32
00:01:43.806 --> 00:01:46.597
Your turn. Say: online order.

33
00:01:49.297 --> 00:01:50.356
online order.

34
00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.363
delivery fee.

35
00:01:53.063 --> 00:01:56.165
delivery fee means money you pay to have something brought to you.

36
00:01:56.465 --> 00:01:59.614
The delivery fee is free for orders over fifty dollars.

37
00:02:00.314 --> 00:02:03.175
Your turn. Say: delivery fee.

38
00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:07.144
delivery fee.

39
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:09.047
store credit.

40
00:02:09.747 --> 00:02:14.811
store credit means money you can only spend in one shop, often given instead of a refund.

41
00:02:15.111 --> 00:02:17.575
The shop gave me store credit instead of cash.

42
00:02:18.275 --> 00:02:20.510
Your turn. Say: store credit.

43
00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:24.454
store credit.

44
00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.461
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:27.761 --> 00:02:31.830
Look at this bag! It was made in Italy, and it's only ten dollars!

46
00:02:33.117 --> 00:02:37.629
Ten dollars? It might be counterfeit. Was it sold by an official store?

47
00:02:38.917 --> 00:02:42.277
I'm not sure. It was recommended by an influencer.

48
00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:46.860
Check the customer reviews and do a price comparison first.

49
00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:52.137
You're right. Most of these bags are produced in big factories.

50
00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:56.869
And remember the delivery fee. Don't make an impulse buy!

51
00:02:58.183 --> 00:03:01.309
Grammar focus: The passive (present and past).

52
00:03:01.609 --> 00:03:05.199
Use the passive when the action is more important than the person who did it.

53
00:03:05.499 --> 00:03:11.785
Present passive: is or are plus past participle. Past passive: was or were plus past participle.

54
00:03:12.085 --> 00:03:17.025
For example: These phones are made in Vietnam. My order was delivered yesterday.

55
00:03:17.325 --> 00:03:22.369
Use the passive when the action is more important than who did it. Add by + person if needed.

56
00:03:23.383 --> 00:03:26.094
Now read and listen. How to Shop Smart Online.

57
00:03:26.394 --> 00:03:30.866
Millions of products are sold online every day in Southeast Asia.

58
00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:35.914
Unfortunately, some of them are counterfeit and of poor quality.

59
00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:41.051
Smart shoppers always read customer reviews and do a price comparison.

60
00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:46.172
Many items can be returned, but sometimes only store credit is given.

61
00:03:47.483 --> 00:03:51.271
Planning your shopping helps you avoid an expensive impulse buy.

62
00:03:52.583 --> 00:03:55.027
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:55.327 --> 00:03:58.000
Something you buy suddenly without planning is an blank.

64
00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.976
A, impulse buy. B, online order. C, store credit.

65
00:04:05.983 --> 00:04:08.180
The answer is A: impulse buy.

66
00:04:09.683 --> 00:04:11.567
This rice blank in Battambang.

67
00:04:11.867 --> 00:04:14.998
A, grows. B, is grown. C, grew.

68
00:04:18.983 --> 00:04:20.878
The answer is B: is grown.

69
00:04:22.383 --> 00:04:24.963
The parcel blank to the wrong address last week.

70
00:04:25.263 --> 00:04:28.255
A, was sent. B, is sent. C, sent.

71
00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.180
The answer is A: was sent.

72
00:04:35.683 --> 00:04:36.963
Fake products are blank.

73
00:04:37.263 --> 00:04:41.706
A, second-hand. B, counterfeit. C, customer reviews.

74
00:04:45.717 --> 00:04:47.472
The answer is B: counterfeit.

75
00:04:48.983 --> 00:04:52.272
According to the text, sometimes shops only give blank.

76
00:04:52.572 --> 00:04:56.202
A, a refund. B, store credit. C, a discount.

77
00:05:00.217 --> 00:05:02.565
The answer is B: store credit.

78
00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:07.921
Now it's your turn to speak. What do you check before you buy something online?

79
00:05:13.221 --> 00:05:19.424
I check the customer reviews, compare prices and make sure the delivery fee is not too high.

80
00:05:19.724 --> 00:05:21.212
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:22.217 --> 00:05:26.866
Great work today! You learned eight new words and the passive (present and past).

82
00:05:27.166 --> 00:05:30.225
Today's value is honesty. Always tell the truth.

83
00:05:30.525 --> 00:05:32.747
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

84
00:05:33.047 --> 00:05:35.607
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

